      "published_at": "2016-01-22",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If it's the turn Eldrazi Aggressor comes under your control, and it loses haste after being declared as an attacker, it will continue to attack. It won't be removed from combat."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d17a1109-3a7f-4a39-b602-155da819235f",
      "published_at": "2019-06-14",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Bellowing Elk’s effect checks each turn whether it applies during that turn. It doesn’t check only during the turn it enters the battlefield."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d17a1109-3a7f-4a39-b602-155da819235f",
      "published_at": "2019-06-14",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Bellowing Elk’s effect applies even if the other creature entered the battlefield under your control before Bellowing Elk entered the battlefield, and it continues to apply even if that creature leaves the battlefield."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "02418479-9455-417f-a6a1-004356faff37",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "This has the mana abilities associated with both of its basic land types."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "02418479-9455-417f-a6a1-004356faff37",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "This has basic land types, but it isn't a basic land. Things that affect basic lands don't affect it. Things that affect basic land types do."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "f9e668f9-21af-4fd8-9a37-6505ab2234e3",
      "published_at": "2021-04-16",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Although you may want to include Lessons in your sideboard if you’re playing with cards that instruct you to learn, Lesson cards can be included in your main deck like other instant or sorcery cards."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "f9e668f9-21af-4fd8-9a37-6505ab2234e3",
      "published_at": "2021-04-16",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Lesson is a spell subtype found on some instant and sorcery cards in the Strixhaven set. The Lesson subtype has no special rules associated with it."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "c6a2e410-b182-48d1-aeb2-bc8de27e9cd2",
      "published_at": "2012-10-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If the target card is no longer in the graveyard when Cremate tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't draw a card."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "c6a2e410-b182-48d1-aeb2-bc8de27e9cd2",
      "published_at": "2012-10-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You must be able to target a card in a graveyard to cast Cremate."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2011-09-22",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type (such as by Sea's Claim), it continues to be a creature and a Dryad."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2013-06-07",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type, it continues to be a green Dryad creature."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Due to its color indicator (appearing to the left of its type line), Dryad Arbor is green. Color indicators apply in all zones, not just the battlefield."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Dryad Arbor is played as a land. It doesn't use the stack, it's not a spell, it can't be responded to, it has no mana cost, and it counts as your land play for the turn."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Forest is a land type and Dryad is a creature type."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If a Dryad Arbor gains flash, or you have the ability to play Dryad Arbor as though it had flash (due to Teferi, Mage of Zhalfir or Scout's Warning, for example), you can ignore the normal timing rules for when during your turn you can play a land, but not any other restrictions. You can't play Dryad Arbor during another player's turn, and you can't play Dryad Arbor if you don't have any land plays remaining."
    }
  ]
